[
  "[SCENE: Camera. Show the 2011 interview frame.]\nThis is The Sound Above. I'm Mike Hall.\nMy first UGtastic interview was with Sergio Pereira.\nWe recorded it at Software Craftsmanship North America in 2011.\nChicago Alt.NET was the first user group I attended.\nIt was also the first one where I gave a talk.\nThat's why I wanted to start this rewatch here.\n[PAUSE]\n[SHOW: Interview frame or Chicago Alt.NET meeting archive.]\n",
  "[SCENE: Camera. Keep the archive nearby.]\nSergio says the group was hard to define.\nHe describes the people who met and the ideas they brought.\nThey were developers who used .NET and wanted to hear ideas from elsewhere too.\nThe group met once a month at Redpoint Technologies in the Sears Tower.\nSergio says a typical meeting had about twenty-five people.\nMembers often brought talks they had already given to their teams at work.\n[FREEFORM: Say what you remember about attending and speaking there. Stay with details you remember.]\n",
  "[SCENE: Camera, then transcript.]\nThe question for this rewatch is small.\nWhat made this group a place where people wanted to come back?\nSergio talks about helping members become speakers.\nHe names NHibernate, CodeSharp, and IronRuby as examples of topics that could use a room.\nHe also says the group was about software development, not only .NET.\n[SHOW: Transcript lines about member talks and the group's audience.]\nI want to hear how that comes across now.\n",
  "[SCENE: Switch to archive tape.]\n[REWATCH: Sergio Pereira interview, start at 00:00.]\nLet the conversation play. Watch for Sergio's own description of the group.\n[FREEFORM: React to the tape. Pause when you have something to say.]\nListen for the monthly schedule, the size of the room, and his invitation to members.\nNotice where the group reached beyond .NET.\n[SCENE: Return to camera.]\n[FREEFORM: What do you remember differently now? What did the tape bring back?]\n",
  "[SCENE: Workbench. Open the interview transcript beside the recording.]\nThe searchable transcript makes this conversation easier to revisit.\nSearch for the part where Sergio talks about members giving presentations.\nThen listen to the full answer on the tape.\nThe transcript helps me find the moment. Sergio's voice gives it the shape.\n[FREEFORM: Compare what you remember with what Sergio says here.]\n",
  "[SCENE: Outro card with Sergio's name and the interview link.]\nThanks for joining me for this rewatch with Sergio Pereira.\nThe full interview transcript and its source links are on just3ws.com.\nChicago Alt.NET was the first user group I attended and the first one where I gave a talk.\nI'm glad Sergio's account is still here for us to hear.\nNext time, Ray Hightower talks about ChicagoRuby.\nUntil then, take care of each other and keep making room to learn.\n"
]